      "author": "Michael michi.fu@quickline.ch",
      "maintainer": "Michael michi.fu@quickline.ch",
      "sentence": "Heap-free typed state store with change callbacks for microcontrollers, using the same struct reflection (REFLECT/MEMBER) as ReflectJSON and ReflectINI.",
      "paragraph": "Declare state variables and their types once with STATE_VARIABLES, then set/get them without template arguments. Change detection for reflected structs, arrays, std::optional and float tolerances; multiple listeners per variable; fixed RAM, no heap, no std::function. Lock policies for dual-core RP2040/RP2350 and ESP32, Teensy interrupts and RTOS tasks. Needs C++17. Free for noncommercial use; commercial use requires a license.",
      "category": "Data Storage",
      "architectures": [
        "*"
